{
  "description": "U8 damage tracking in the compositor (#220): CPU per shown frame, shown frames per second, CPU per second and memory with frames without a change skipped (Skip, the default) and with every frame composited and shown (Off, BL_DAMAGE=0), both on the same engine (site 0, main with U8; both count only frames with a change), and the engine before U8 (E0, site 1, counts every frame) for the correction check. Pages: CSS animation, 360p video, WebGL and scrolling (every frame changes the whole view), plus idle (an animation outside the view, nothing visible changes: only CPU per second, frames.mjs reports no frame rate there). Rule R under SwiftShader (owner decision, no device with a real GPU); the lever is CPU per second on idle (not part of the plan's U8 measurement, which names anim and video360; to be confirmed by the owner), the other pages may not get worse (rule correction). Perf run 39644894451 measured this plan with a third arm, Target (BL_DAMAGE=target, only the damage composited into a texture per view), which failed the correction and was removed. engine_runs: <U8 run>,<run before U8>",
